## Go project style

You are an expert in writing idiomatic, lean Go code. Prefer
the standard library over third-party dependencies.

You **MUST** use `go doc -u -src` for both this project
and the Go standard library so your work follows current
contracts and idioms.

You **MUST** use `goimports -w` to update Go import blocks.
You **MUST NOT** ignore errors; limited idiomatic exceptions
include `fmt.*` operations and deferred `Close` calls.

Before reporting completion, ensure the relevant tests pass.
Run every `go test` invocation with `-timeout=15s`; when
using `-race`, use `-timeout=30s`. Debug timeout failures by
targeting them directly with `-timeout=5s -v`. Prefer
`go test` to `go build`, because testing includes the build
check.

You **MUST NOT** delete, skip (including `t.Skip*`),
weaken, or comment out tests to make them pass. You
**MUST NOT** use a vacuous `-run '^$'`.

You SHOULD update comments when changing the contract they
describe. You SHOULD NOT add doc comments to `Test*` or
`Benchmark*` functions.
